From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: Change Icon dialog, multi-file Properties, Format drive dialog, network address control

shell32: Change Icon dialog, multi-file Properties, Format drive dialog, network address control

PickIconDlg shows the Change Icon dialog: the icons of a file (environment
variables expanded; empty or no icons lists shell32.dll) in an owner-drawn list,
Browse, OK/Cancel; the path buffer gets the file as typed and the index the icon.

SHMultiFileProperties opens a Properties sheet for several file system objects:
count, common type and location, total size and contents, attributes as tri-state
check boxes applied to all items on OK, plus "*" property sheet extensions.

SHFormatDrive shows the Format dialog for fixed/removable drives backed by a block
device (resolved through /proc/self/mountinfo; the root file system and non-device
mounts are not formattable). Start asks for confirmation, then sends the sg-admind
"format" verb (spool request: device, file system, label, quick, unit size).
Returns the default format ID after a format, SHFMT_CANCEL otherwise,
SHFMT_NOFORMAT/SHFMT_ERROR as documented.

InitNetworkAddressControl registers the msctls_netaddress class (an Edit
superclass) with NCM_GETADDRESS (ParseNetworkString under the allowed types),
NCM_SETALLOWTYPE/GETALLOWTYPE and NCM_DISPLAYERRORTIP.
